# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the multithreaded API tests (test/api/mt,
# label "mt"; preset tsan-mt, workflow tsan-mt.yml).
#
# Each entry is a known race of the engine built for several threads (the
# tsan-mt preset), under a "# <inventory ids> (P<n>): ..."
# comment that names its ids in the inventory of the thread-safety design and
# the PR of its plan that removes it (the workflow's summary reads that
# comment). The PR that fixes a race deletes its entries, so the job then
# fails if the race is still there; a race not listed here fails its test.

# L2 (P12): a false positive inside ICU, kept. Every RegexMatcher that
# unicode::regex creates (one per regex, never shared) starts on ICU's empty
# UText RegexStaticSets::gStaticSets->fEmptyText, a 144-byte UText that the
# first thread to compile a regex allocates in ICU's one-time initialization;
# the other threads clone it (memcpy in shallowTextClone) after reading the
# init-once state with an atomic load. ICU is not built with TSan, so that
# atomic is invisible and the clone is reported as racing with the malloc.
# Nothing is written to the UText after its initialization.
race:shallowTextClone
